@nsobid-03FF4A3BEC96BDE3A2E37CE3AA4CAA0CAE8935A8

# Rhythm Heaven Groove 1.0.0 - 3840x2160 resolution

// Rhythm Heaven Groove runs on a bespoke Nintendo engine that talks to NVN
// and nn::vi directly.  It draws the whole frame into one offscreen render
// target and then blits that into the scan buffer, so there are two sizes:
//
//   1. the scan buffer -- what reaches the display, i.e. screenshot size,
//   2. the scene render target -- the actual internal resolution.
//
// (2) is handled by intercepting the engine's single render-texture creation
// wrapper and scaling every sufficiently large request.  This is deliberately
// proportional rather than a fixed size: RenderDoc showed stages render into
// targets of their own native size (one at 1000x900, the main one at
// 1920x1080), so a fixed rewrite only caught some of them.
//
// The engine keeps a render target's design UNITS separate from its pixel
// size and only the pixels change here, so coordinate space, UI layout and
// camera are untouched -- only pixel density moves.

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the render and scan-out resolution to 3840x2160
// (4.00x the pixels of the native 1920x1080).

@enabled
// 1. Scan buffer: the packed `height<<32 | width` constant the graphics
//    device constructor stores at device+0x28.
0050CBDC 08E081D2
0050CBE8 080EC1F2
// 2. Render-texture creation wrapper: scale every render texture wider
//    than 512px by 2.0x.  Stages have their own native sizes (a
//    capture showed one at 1000x900), so an exact 1920x1080 match was too
//    narrow -- this scales whatever the engine asks for.  Small textures
//    (glyph atlases, gradient LUTs) stay untouched.  One CMP drives both
//    selects; the engine's own MOV W19,W1 and MOV W20,W0 sit between these
//    lines untouched and now read the rescaled registers.
004F5848 1F000871   // CMP  W0, #512
004F584C 2800010B   // scaled height -> W8
004F5850 01A1811A   // CSEL W1, W8, W1, GE
004F5858 0800000B   // scaled width  -> W8
004F585C 00A1801A   // CSEL W0, W8, W0, GE
@stop

// Reverse-engineered against the game's own renderer, with the frame
// structure confirmed by RenderDoc capture.  Every offset byte-verified.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
